I.K.E. Windows engine: what the two integrations need inside Qt WebEngine

Neither Vivaldi nor Cromite is built the way I.K.E.'s engine is (Qt WebEngine,
FFmpeg with ffmpeg_branding="Chromium"). Four small changes, written for
I.K.E., each marked "I.K.E.:" in the source:

Qt WebEngine:
  content/gpu/in_process_gpu_thread.cc   COM on the thread that runs the GPU
      and media services inside the browser process (a GPU process of its own
      initialises COM in gpu_main.cc); MediaFoundationAudioDecoder needs it.
  media/filters/win/media_foundation_audio_decoder.cc   PumpOutput() tested
      an HRESULT with "!"; fixed in later Chromium versions. Without it a
      change of the output format (HE-AAC) is an error.

FFmpeg without an AAC decoder or parser (plain MP4 files, not Media Source):
  media/ffmpeg/ffmpeg_common.cc     AAC gets a sample format although FFmpeg
      did not fill one in (as Chromium already does for AC3).
  media/filters/ffmpeg_demuxer.cc   the AAC profile, which the ADTS header
      needs, is read from the AudioSpecificConfig when FFmpeg left it unknown.

Licence: BSD-3-Clause, as the Chromium files they change (two of those files
are also changed by the Cromite patch, 0003).

diff --git a/chromium/content/gpu/in_process_gpu_thread.cc b/chromium/content/gpu/in_process_gpu_thread.cc
index 9ca23324..0a740afa 100644
--- a/chromium/content/gpu/in_process_gpu_thread.cc
+++ b/chromium/content/gpu/in_process_gpu_thread.cc
@@ -67,7 +67,16 @@ InProcessGpuThread::InProcessGpuThread(
     : base::Thread("Chrome_InProcGpuThread"),
       params_(params),
       gpu_process_(nullptr),
-      gpu_preferences_(gpu_preferences) {}
+      gpu_preferences_(gpu_preferences) {
+#if BUILDFLAG(IS_WIN)
+  // I.K.E.: Qt WebEngine runs the GPU service on this thread, inside the
+  // browser process, and the media service with it. Media Foundation needs
+  // COM to create a decoder (MediaFoundationAudioDecoder: MFTEnumEx and
+  // IMFActivate::ActivateObject). A GPU process of its own initialises COM in
+  // content/gpu/gpu_main.cc, as a multi-threaded apartment; the same here.
+  init_com_with_mta(true);
+#endif
+}
 
 InProcessGpuThread::~InProcessGpuThread() {
   Stop();
